{"availability":"available","full":"cagscalclabs/lwip-ce","name":"lwip-ce","description":"An IP stack implementation for the TI-84+ CE derived from lwIP code. Implements custom memory management for <60K RAM, assembly optimizations, and a custom lightweight TLS stack engineered for the constraints of the system.","category":"Developer tools","language":"C","stars":27,"forks":4,"created":"2023-11-05T01:41:42Z","updated":"2026-10-09T05:03:38Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"https://cagscalclabs.github.io/lwip-ce/","topics":["networking","ti-84-plus-ce","tls13"],"demo":"https://cagscalclabs.github.io/lwip-ce/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:57:02.328Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T08:57:02.328Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T08:57:02.328Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:50.963Z","stars":27,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-09T08:57:02.328Z","stars":27,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SAST uses git diff against upstream lwIP to filter out untouched upstream code and scans only targets unique to this repository. For upstream issues, file an issue with nonGNU.","DAST uses a locally-run hardware-in-the-loop workflow because the current emulator does not support Ethernet devices. A helper program runs on the calculator and exposes the DAST target while a local script attaches to it, performs network probes, advances the calculator-side test state, and writes results to JSON. This workflow then parses the JSON report and updates the test state accordingly.","Timing analysis checks for secret-dependent timing leaks: it samples repeated runs of a primitive across input classes designed to exercise different internal code paths (e.g. a bad MAC vs. a good one), then looks for variance in runtime that tracks the input class rather than noise. Some allowance is given for CPU jitter, computed via MAD-based sigma over the baseline class. This test does not prove the absence of secret-dependent timing leaks, but it provides statistical evidence that runtime stays consistent across all classes of input."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cagscalclabs/lwip-ce/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"869bec4e7d0b208f82d7e33441f12df28d8051f9b9f3cd8539e5b6d7cc48695b","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:45:17.549Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:45:17.549Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"SAST uses git diff against upstream lwIP to filter out untouched upstream code and scans only targets unique to this repository. For upstream issues, file an issue with nonGNU.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cagscalclabs/lwip-ce/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"869bec4e7d0b208f82d7e33441f12df28d8051f9b9f3cd8539e5b6d7cc48695b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cagscalclabs/lwip-ce/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:45:17.550Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T05:03:38Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cagscalclabs/lwip-ce/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:45:17.550Z","hash":"869bec4e7d0b208f82d7e33441f12df28d8051f9b9f3cd8539e5b6d7cc48695b","originalBytes":4749,"storedBytes":4749,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["test","lwip","cavp","against","dast","nist","primitive","samples","timing","upstream","api","appvar","calculator","code","does","ethernet","lwip-ce","runs","socket","tcp","tls","validation","workflow","across","app-facing","checks","classes","doc","driver","dynamic","input","leaks","libload","library","main","network","nongnu","one","output","over","primitives","quality","readme","rsp","runtime","sast","secret-dependent","see","selects","sha-256","site","small","stack","state","stays","ti-84+","udp","usb","uses","whitepaper","absence","accordingly.","advanced","advances","aes-cbc","allocator","allowance","analysis","api.","architecture","attaches","auditing.","available","back","bad","baseline","because","beta","both","bu